{"Title":"An Act permitting ambulances to transport patients to urgent care centers ","BillNumber":"H2238","DocketNumber":"HD366","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T14:33:05.253"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T14:33:05.2533333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2238/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Mirra of Georgetown, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2238) of Lenny Mirra relative to permitting ambulances to transport patients to urgent care centers.  Public Health.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 2 of Chapter 111C of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting at the end thereof the following new paragraph:-\r\n\t(17) in situations determined as non-emergency, permit the transportation of patients directly to a clinic, as defined in section 52 of chapter 111, including an urgent care center, instead of an emergency department.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J16","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J16"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}